# Test: Invalid ig:confidenceLevel datatype usage
# This test validates that ig:confidenceLevel must be xsd:decimal
# Should FAIL with: "ig:confidenceLevel must be xsd:decimal datatype"

@prefix ex:  <http://example.org/> .
@prefix ig:  <http://tio.models.tmforum.org/tio/v3.6.0/IntentGuaranteeOntology/> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

################################################################################
# VIOLATION: ig:confidenceLevel with wrong datatype
#
# The ig:confidenceLevel property MUST be xsd:decimal (typically 0.0 to 1.0)
# Common mistakes: using strings, integers, or untyped literals
################################################################################

# WRONG - using plain string
ex:wrong_confidence_string
  ig:confidenceLevel "high" .

# WRONG - using integer instead of decimal
ex:wrong_confidence_int
  ig:confidenceLevel 95 .

# WRONG - using untyped string that looks like a decimal
ex:wrong_confidence_untyped
  ig:confidenceLevel "0.95" .
